WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.122
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03.172 --> 00:00:05.816
AI for Teens, video 5.

3
00:00:05.866 --> 00:00:09.000
Metrics beyond “accuracy”.

4
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:15.990
When classes are imbalanced, ninety-five percent accuracy can hide a useless model.

5
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:21.997
A confusion matrix shows predicted versus actual labels.

6
00:00:22.047 --> 00:00:25.940
It makes false alarms and missed cases visible.

7
00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:32.432
Precision asks: of the alarms we raised, how many were real?

8
00:00:32.482 --> 00:00:37.140
Recall asks: of the real cases, how many did we catch?

9
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:43.335
If ninety-eight of one hundred transactions are normal, a model that always

10
00:00:43.385 --> 00:00:47.810
says normal is ninety-eight percent accurate and catches zero fraud.

11
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.610
Let us recap.

12
00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:54.794
Accuracy can mislead on imbalanced data.

13
00:00:54.844 --> 00:00:58.665
Choose metrics from real-world costs.

14
00:00:58.715 --> 00:01:02.640
Next: Bias: find it, fix what you can.
